> Can I do a Reverse Proxy on Dreamhost?
**assistant**:
> Yes, you can set up a reverse proxy on DreamHost, but it depends on the type of hosting plan you have. Here are the steps and considerations:
> 
> ### Step 1: Check Your Hosting Plan
> 
> - **VPS or Dedicated Server:** You can set up a reverse proxy using Apache or Nginx if you have a Virtual Private Server (VPS) or a Dedicated Server.
> - **Shared Hosting:** DreamHost's shared hosting plans typically do not allow the installation of custom server configurations or modules, so setting up a reverse proxy via shared hosting would not be possible.
> 
> ### Step 2: Setting Up a Reverse Proxy on VPS or Dedicated Server
> 
> - **For Apache:**
>   1. **Enable Proxy Modules:**
>      Make sure the `proxy` and `proxy_http` modules are enabled. You can do this by running:
>      ```bash
>      sudo a2enmod proxy
>      sudo a2enmod proxy_http
>      sudo systemctl restart apache2
>      ```
> 
>   2. **Edit Your Apache Configuration:**
>      Open your site's configuration file:
>      ```bash
>      sudo nano /etc/apache2/sites-available/your-site.conf
>      ```
>      Add the reverse proxy configuration as previously outlined:
> 
>      ```apache
>      <VirtualHost *:80>
>          ServerName matchedbyjo.com
> 
>          ProxyPreserveHost On
>          ProxyPass / https://matchedbyjo.my.canva.site/matched-by-jo/
>          ProxyPassReverse / https://matchedbyjo.my.canva.site/matched-by-jo/
>      </VirtualHost>
>      ```
> 
>   3. **Restart Apache:**
>      ```bash
>      sudo systemctl restart apache2
>      ```
> 
> - **For Nginx:**
>   1. **Edit Your Nginx Configuration:**
>      Open your site's configuration file:
>      ```bash
>      sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/your-site
>      ```
>      Add the following configuration:
> 
>      ```nginx
>      server {
>          listen 80;
>          server_name matchedbyjo.com;
> 
>          location / {
>              proxy_pass https://matchedbyjo.my.canva.site/matched-by-jo;
>              proxy_set_header Host $host;
>              proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
>              proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
>              proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
>          }
>      }
>      ```
> 
>   2. **Restart Nginx:**
>      ```bash
>      sudo systemctl restart nginx
>      ```
> 
> ### Step 3: SSL Configuration (Optional)
> 
> If you want to handle SSL, you can either use Let's Encrypt or configure your SSL certificate. You will want to set up the certificates and update the configuration to listen on port 443.
> 
> ### Final Step: Test Your Setup
> 
> After making these changes, test `matchedbyjo.com` to see if it displays the content from `https://matchedbyjo.my.canva.site/matched-by-jo` while keeping `matchedbyjo.com` in the address bar.
> 
> ### Additional Notes
> 
> - If you're unsure about making these configurations, you could consider reaching out to DreamHost support for guidance specific to your hosting plan.
> - Keep in mind that with shared hosting you are quite limited, and using a VPS or dedicated server is generally more flexible for advanced configurations.
